B.a3f=new A.m5("Where the content comes from","NICE guidelines \xb7 the Egyptian National Drug Formulary \xb7 the Egyptian Essential Medicines List \xb7 the BNF and BNF for Children \xb7 WHO model formularies \xb7 disease-specific society guidance such as IDSA and GOLD.\n\nEvery condition page lists the specific sources behind it. Where we could not source something, the app says so instead of filling the gap.",null)
B.a3g=new A.m5("The scores and calculators","The clinical scores \u2014 Centor, Wells, PHQ-9, CHA\u2082DS\u2082-VASc, the Ottawa rules and the rest \u2014 apply exactly the criteria their published source states, and output a risk band and what that source says to do. They never output a drug dose. Each shows its criteria and its citation on the same screen.\n\nBMI and Albak Amana are the same: arithmetic you could do yourself, and a chart lookup, both naming their source.\n\nA child\u2019s dose is shown as the published mg/kg rule, with that rule worked out at four fixed weights beneath it. Those four figures are our arithmetic on the printed rule, not a table quoted from a guideline, and the screen says so. There is no box to type a weight into.",null)
B.a3h=new A.m5("Your data stays on this phone","The app holds no account and sends nothing anywhere. Your favourites, your recent lookups, the brands you marked as unavailable and anything you type into a calculator are stored on this device only, and are deleted with the app.\n\nNothing you enter about a patient is recorded, and no patient identity is asked for anywhere.\n\nThis is a reference for prescribers. It is not a medical device and it does not diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any condition \u2014 it reports what named guidelines say, and the clinical decision remains yours.",null)
B.a3i=new A.m5("Prices and brands","Egyptian trade names and prices come from the national drug register. Prices move and the register lags behind the pharmacy shelf, so treat every figure as an indication, not a quotation. A product being listed does not mean it is in stock, and a product being absent does not mean it is gone.",null)
B.a3j=new A.m5('What "verified" means here \u2014 and what it does not','Every dose in this app was checked against a named clinical guideline, and the guideline is shown beside the dose so you can go and read it.\n\nThat is all "verified" means. It does NOT mean a doctor has reviewed and signed off this content. No clinician has. Where you would normally trust a reference book because a named editor stood behind it, here you should trust the citation and check it when it matters.',null)
B.a3k=new A.m5("Reporting something wrong","If a dose here does not match the guideline it cites, that is a defect and it matters more than any feature. Note the condition and the drug and report it.",null)
